From: XProtocol Bot
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Release only the locked window data in WindowPosChanged.

wine-wayland's "Make window lock mutex recursive" took the owner's data with
wayland_win_data_get() and released it at the end of WAYLAND_WindowPosChanged.
The wineland child-rendering series then looks the owner up with
wayland_win_data_get_nolock() again, but the release stayed: every call with an
owner unlocked win_data_mutex once more than it locked it. On a recursive mutex
that drops a caller's outer hold early (another thread can take the lock while
the caller still uses window data), and the caller's own release later fails.
owner_data and toplevel_data are looked up under the lock taken for data; only
that one is released.
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1053,7 +1053,8 @@
         wayland_win_data_update_wayland_state(data);
     }
 
-    if (owner_data) wayland_win_data_release(owner_data);
+    /* owner_data and toplevel_data come from wayland_win_data_get_nolock(), under the
+     * lock taken for data: only that one is released. */
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
 }
 
